  "answer_text": "The name **Glenwood Pool** can refer to several different swimming destinations, but it most famously refers to the historic hot springs resort in Colorado. \n\n---\n\n### 1. Glenwood Hot Springs Pool (Glenwood Springs, Colorado)\nThis is the most famous \"Glenwood Pool\" in the world. Established in 1888, it is **the world's largest outdoor mineral hot springs pool**.\n* **The Water:** Geothermal water flows from the on-site Yampah Spring (\"Big Medicine\" in the Ute language) at an incredibly hot 122\u00b0F (50\u00b0C). The water is rich in 15 different naturally occurring minerals and is cooled before reaching the swimming pools.\n* **The Pools:**\n  * **The Grand Pool:** Kept at a comfortable 90\u00b0\u201393\u00b0F (32\u00b0\u201334\u00b0C). It is over two city blocks long and is designed for swimming, playing, and relaxing.\n  * **The Therapy Pool:** Kept at a hotter 104\u00b0F (40\u00b0C) for maximum relaxation and physical therapy.\n  * **Yampah Mineral Baths:** A newly designed area featuring multi-temperature soaking experiences.\n  * **Sopris Splash Zone:** A family-friendly area with water slides, a lazy river, and interactive water features (open during the warmer months).\n* **When to Visit:** It is open year-round, rain or shine. Visiting during the winter while snow falls around the hot water is a highly popular experience.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Community \"Glenwood\" Pools\nIf you are looking for a local neighborhood pool, you might be thinking of one of the following:\n\n* **Glenwood Pool (Forest Glen, Maryland):** A private, member-owned community swim club nestled in a wooded area in Silver Spring/Forest Glen, MD. It is highly popular with local families and features a swim team.\n* **Glenwood Park Pool (Atlanta, Georgia):** A neighborhood 6-lane, Junior Olympic-sized saline pool and fitness center located in the Glenwood Park community.\n* **Glenwood Pool (Columbus, Ohio):** A public outdoor pool operated by the Columbus Recreation and Parks Department, which is free to access with a local leisure card.\n\n*If you are looking for specific details (like hours, pricing, or membership details) for one of these pools, please let me know which location you are referring to!*",
